  "$comment": "Slots for scripts/web-compose.py. Kind 'scene' exports an illustrated environment (Light and Dusk) at the page's widths, with an optional phone-width crop and a foreground cut-out. Kind 'iphone' renders a 3D iPhone with a real screenshot, lit by the named lighting preset for each mode (Light scenes show the Light screenshot, Dusk scenes the Dark one). Kind 'spot' crops a small illustration out of a scene. Screens are looked up in art/web/screens/{dark,light}/ first, then in the CI folders below (Dark falls back to Light).",
